      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To begin structuring your data, you should focus on logging the \"spikes\" as discrete events. For each instance, record the precise time of the spike, a detailed description of the predicted event, and what you perceived as the certainty level (e.g., a score from 1 to 10). Crucially, you must also record the actual outcome and the exact time it occurred. This paired data structure allows you to quantify the lead time between your prediction and the event.",
